<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech fund IKS PLUS posts 1996 net loss.</title>
<headline>Czech fund IKS PLUS posts 1996 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech closed-end mutual fund PF IKS KB PLUS, managed by the investment arm of Komercni Banka a.s., said on Thursday it recorded a 525 million crown audited loss last year, after a 102 million net profit in 1995.</p>
<p> Net result			525.03 loss  vs    102.24 profit</p>
<p>Result from financial</p>
<p> operations			458.92 loss  vs    148.82 profit</p>
<p> Operating result		 55.10 loss  vs     45.58 profit</p>
<p> Total assets		  1,895.91	 vs  1,570.07</p>
<p>Note. Results are for year ending December 31, 1995. All figures are in millions of crowns. The fund's units are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. The fund has said the loss was created by an accounting operation bringing the portfolio book value of shares to real levels from nominal prices.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
